From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: [PATCH] m2ts_filter: keep the initial PID list sorted (PG before IG)

m2ts_filter_init() fills the wipe list with video, audio, IG (0x1400..)
and then PG (0x1200..) PIDs, but _pid_in_list() stops at the first entry
larger than the PID it looks for, so no PG PID was ever found: at every
playitem start inside a clip the presentation-graphics streams bypassed
the in-time cut and the previous playitem's subtitle display sets reached
the player. After a seek the list is rebuilt through _add_pid(), which
sorts, so there PG was cut - playitem starts now behave like seeks.

Present in libbluray 1.5.0, 1.5.1 and master.

--- a/src/libbluray/decoders/m2ts_filter.c
+++ b/src/libbluray/decoders/m2ts_filter.c
@@ -92,12 +92,14 @@ M2TS_FILTER *m2ts_filter_init(int64_t in_pts, int64_t out_pts,
         for (ii = 0; ii < num_audio; ii++) {
             pid[npid++] = HDMV_PID_AUDIO_FIRST + ii;
         }
-        for (ii = 0; ii < num_ig; ii++) {
-            pid[npid++] = HDMV_PID_IG_FIRST + ii;
-        }
+        /* PG (0x1200..) before IG (0x1400..): the lists must stay sorted,
+         * _pid_in_list() stops at the first larger PID */
         for (ii = 0; ii < num_pg; ii++) {
             pid[npid++] = HDMV_PID_PG_FIRST + ii;
         }
+        for (ii = 0; ii < num_ig; ii++) {
+            pid[npid++] = HDMV_PID_IG_FIRST + ii;
+        }
     }
 
     return p;
